body:
- **P6 — CLI board, wait/last, verify** (cli). No ARIA. trycmd / assert_cmd assert the non-TTY modes, and the portable-pty outer PTY asserts the TTY-only behaviours, on `ubuntu-latest`:
  - linear static output: under the outer PTY, `waiting: <name>` appears exactly once on stderr and the stream contains no `\r` redraw, cursor-movement or erase sequence (no spinner); under non-TTY the `waiting:` line is absent;
  - `[NN/NN] … pass|fail`;
  - **cli mirror:** a literal pins the caption order the deferred 0.2.0 page must share (NAME · LIVE · STATUS · WHEEL · DIALOG · CLI), not a trycmd case: the `CAPTION` literal in the root case `list_human_board_is_the_literal_rows` (`tests/cli_list.rs`) and the unit case `board_row_caption_and_default_row_are_the_literals` (`src/human/board/`), chunk 2026-10-11-the-board-viola-list.
  - no SGR under non-TTY / `NO_COLOR` / `TERM=dumb` / `--json`;
  - under the outer PTY, every SGR span sits beside its word (amber only on `DIALOG`, dim only on stale rows, bold only on NAME column values), and `unable` / `fail` carry no SGR; as built (chunk 2026-10-17-cli-output-discipline) `viola list`'s spans are checked under the outer PTY by `cross_list_rows_style_each_span_beside_its_word_on_a_terminal` (bold NAME, amber only on `DIALOG`) and at the unit tier by the `board_row_style_*` cases; dim only on stale rows is proven at the unit tier (`board_row_style_a_stale_row_is_dim_end_to_end_and_only_dialog_is_amber`) and under the outer PTY (the stale-row witness, below); `viola wait` and `viola --help` carry no ESC byte and no lone CR (`tests/support/sgr.rs` `redraws`);
  - C0/C1 escaped (security excerpt, C0/C1 escaping; ratified T5 for `list` rows), checked with assert_cmd on `ubuntu-latest`:
    - Setup: human-mode `viola wait` / `viola last` run against a `viola-fake-agent` event whose text carries C0 and C1 control bytes (including ESC / CSI), and `viola list` runs against a `claude agents --json` fixture row carrying the same bytes plus `\n` / `\t`. As built (chunk 2026-10-16-unwrapped-sessions-on-the-board) `viola list` makes one `claude agents --json` read and prints every unwrapped NAME (the row's `sessionId`, never a `ViolaName`) through `escape_row` on one line, held by the `board_row_*` units and by `tests/cross_list_rows.rs` in three modes (piped, `NO_COLOR` / `TERM=dumb`, the outer PTY; the no-ESC assertion in each mode); beside them the row escape is held by unit cases on a recorded CLI version carrying ESC, C1, DEL, `\n` and `\t`, each printed as `\xHH` (`escape_row_shows_every_control_character_as_hex_text`, `board_row_cli_cell`), and the root cases `list_human_board_is_the_literal_rows` and `list_of_a_stopped_wrapper_is_an_empty_board` assert no ESC and no non-ASCII byte on either stream.
    - Pass condition: each injected control appears only in escaped form. In `wait` / `last` text `\n` / `\t` stay raw. In `list` table rows `\n` / `\t` are escaped too (`\x0A`, `\x09`), so every row stays one fixed-width line.
    - Under non-TTY, `wait` / `last` stdout contains no raw C0 / C1 byte other than `\n` / `\t`, and `list` stdout contains none inside a row. Under the outer PTY, the injected controls are escaped, and viola's own SGR stays beside its word only.
  - These stand in for SC 1.3.2, 1.4.1 and 3.3.1, with no conformance claim.

- **Product type.** Hybrid local developer tool made of three parts:
  - a native Linux CLI binary;
  - a Claude Code plugin (hooks + stdio MCP server) that calls that binary;
  - a minimal view-only frontend, deferred to 0.2.0; its technology is not chosen.

- Test-only binaries, never in a release build: `viola-fake-agent` (a `[[bin]]` of the root package behind feature `fake-agent`, the stand-in `claude`; its print mode `-p <prompt>` / `--print <prompt>` writes its start receipts, fires the SessionStart, UserPromptSubmit (prompt set), Stop and SessionEnd `default` fixtures, prints `ok` on stdout and exits 0, never raw and never reading stdin — the mode `viola verify`'s print probe drives in CI; thirteen argv options (the count's rule is this list), no env, of which nine serve verify's interactive runs and their tests: `--trusted-root <DIR>` (an ancestor walk, both paths canonicalised), `--screens` (writes `Screen.modal` when untrusted, no hook fired, or `Screen.ready` when trusted, SessionStart as before: a clear, then rows joined by CRLF), `--turn-stop` (a submit fires UserPromptSubmit, then Stop, then writes `Screen.turn`), `--dialogs` (a pasted compiled dialog prompt replays its recorded `<stem>-<n>` variants in claim order: a call's PreToolUse fires first; with no decision, its PermissionRequest fires; a decision from either fires its PostToolUse), `--framing` (a pasted compiled paste text fires its recorded `paste-1` / `paste-2` / `paste-3` UserPromptSubmit variant with its bytes unchanged, a new stem reached through `ledger::framing_stem` with no option added, the probed local command fires the recorded `clear-1` SessionEnd then SessionStart and no UserPromptSubmit, and `/compact` fires the recorded `SessionStart.compact-1` with `session_id` set to the last SessionStart the agent fired (the launch one or a replayed clear's; only a SessionStart whose fixture exists moves it) and no UserPromptSubmit;
 a set without a variant fires nothing for it) and the two test-only holds `--stop-receipt-hold-ms <n>` (capped at 1 000 ms, a hold of the Stop hook's receipt that forces a race window open) and `--paste-hint-ms <ms>` (capped at 10 000 ms; with `--framing`, after the long text's replay and its Stop the screen is cleared and `Screen.turn` is drawn only after the hold), and the test-only screen switch `--tag-turn-screen <phase>` (with `--framing` and `--turn-stop`: after the turn of the compiled tag-like paste, and after no other turn, `Screen.<phase>` of the set is drawn in place of `Screen.turn`; a missing file draws nothing), and the test-only screen switch `--long-turn-screen <phase>` (with `--framing` and `--turn-stop`: after the long paste's turn alone, after its Stop, `Screen.<phase>` of the set is drawn in place of `Screen.turn`), and two serve `viola revive`'s tests and, under the fake agent, verify's Run E: `--resume <id>` (the SessionStart fired at launch is the set's recorded `SessionStart.resume-1.json` when the set holds it (`RESUME_VARIANT`, `launch_variant`; 2.1.287 since chunk 2026-10-14-resume-and-compact-ledger-rows), else its recorded `SessionStart.default` payload, with `source` set to `resume` and `session_id` set to the id given, the trailing newline kept) and `--fork-session` (beside `--resume`, `session_id` is the compiled id `0f0e0d0c-0b0a-4908-8706-050403020100`; alone it changes nothing); without `--resume` every payload is the recorded bytes; and two serve the statusline tests: `--settings <file>` and `--statusline-stdin <file>` (with both, and only when the settings file's `statusLine` command, split on ASCII white space, is an absolute command, it runs that command with the stdin file's bytes and files a `statusline` receipt, the `hook` receipt's fields without `event`);
 `--framing` with `--settings <file>` alone replays the set's recorded status line the same way, the one word exactly `"$0"` handed over as `/bin/sh`, spawned directly and never through a shell: `StatusLine.default-1.json` after the launch SessionStart's hooks and `StatusLine.rate-limits-1.json` once at the end of the first Stop's turn, after the turn screen (a relative command is receipted and never run; a set without the variants fires nothing; no option added); beside the options it takes two mode words: `statusline-echo`, which prints its output and files its stdin and exits with the code after the marker path, and `agents` (chunk 2026-10-16-unwrapped-sessions-on-the-board), which answers `agents --json` from files beside its own executable: `agents-mode` (`recorded` · `oversize` · `malformed`, absent read as `recorded`), `agents-rows.json` (planted rows, printed unchanged) and a live `sessions/<pid>.json` registry its interactive runs write (a row written just before its launch SessionStart fires, its `cwd` the launch fixture's recorded `cwd`, `~` without one; a dead or reused pid left out through one `viola_state::liveness::start_times()` read); no option and no env are added (the founder's own answer to P4 fork 2, that chunk's `inputs#I1`)) and `viola-harness` (in `viola-e2e`, behind `scripts/agent-run.sh`; its command contract is test-plan §3) and `viola-mcp-tap` (a `[[bin]]` of `viola-e2e` that records a live MCP exchange for the `Mcp.` fixtures, Repository below: `record <capture> <viola exe> <args…>` is a direct spawn, no shell and no PATH lookup, each line read through `take(MAX_FRAME)` and appended once, tagged with its direction, to a capture created 0600, exiting with the child;
 `fixture <capture> <out>` keeps the client frames up to and including the first `tools/list` request and each request's result keyed by method, through `ledger::scrub` (the home → `~`, the user word → `<user>`) and then `ledger::screen_fault` over every string and key, refusing with the file name and one closed code `home-path` · `absolute-path` · `username` · `email`, never the content).

- **Required telemetry signal:** Fault telemetry per class:
  - torn ndjson line healed, with file and offset;
  - corrupt or unsupported-`v` snapshot → replay recovery;
  - child exit detected on the process handle without EOF;
  - endpoint vanished during `wait` (exit 21 / `instance-unreachable`, `detail` `endpoint-lost`, `during` `call`);
  - stale heartbeat vs live pid.

  These need `event` values or an additive `detail` field (section 3, gap b).

- **Required telemetry signal:** One file sink and line schema on Linux (any current distribution, CI on `ubuntu-latest`), each field fixed:
  - permission application: Unix 0600/0700;
  - append atomicity with concurrent hook writers: POSIX `O_APPEND`;
  - the Unix socket in channel logs;
  - openpty in `pty` spans;
  - the server check's reads: the peer pid by `SO_PEERCRED` and the peer euid by `peer_creds` (a mismatch of either reads `server-verify-failed`; an unreadable euid is refused).

  No OS-specific exporter.

- **Required span attributes:**
  - `run.start`: `instance`;
  - `run.collision_check`: `outcome` (`free|already-live|squatted-name`) — a `live` or `stale` holder is `already-live`; a `gone` one is `free` (taken over, its `events.ndjson` appended to); over a replayed snapshot, which carries no pid or start time, the heartbeat alone decides (a beat no older than `STALE_AFTER` is `already-live`, an older one `free`), and an absent snapshot or a failed read is `free`;
  - `run.pin_copy`: `outcome` (`ok|pinned-hash-mismatch`);
  - `run.conpty_sideload` (Windows): `outcome` (`loaded|hash-mismatch|strict-modes-failed|unreadable|load-failed|not-built`; `strict-modes-failed` when the owner/DACL check refuses the `conpty/` dir or a companion, `PinError::StrictModes`, nothing written), `search_restricted` (bool) — never a refusal and never an exit change: any outcome but `loaded` leaves the child on the inbox ConPTY; never the companions' paths or hashes (D-36);
  - `run.version_gate`: `cli_version`, `cli_verified`;
  - `channel.bind`: `endpoint_kind` (`unix-socket`);
  - `state.snapshot_write`: `v`;
  - `pty.spawn`: `pty_backend` (`openpty`, from `viola_pty::pty_backend()`), `env_stripped_count`.
  - Never the endpoint name, `pinned_bin` path or env values.

- **Required log fields:** common fields plus:
  - `channel-request{corr:<id>, conn, method, from, from_trust:"self-reported", sender}`;
  - `send-issued{corr:<cursor>, from, text_bytes}`, `text_bytes` the same typed-text length as on the span;
  - hook: `hook-invoked{hook_event:"user-prompt-submit", corr:null}` for an ordinary send; `hook-invoked{hook_event:"session-start", corr:null}` for a `/clear` confirmed by its new session or a `/compact` confirmed by its same session (verified CLI), no new event, detail or field (as landed, `src/cmd/hook.rs`: every hook invocation logs `hook-invoked` with its own `hook_event`; the line was not read on this path); an unconfirmable send waits for no hook line;
  - `send-confirmed{corr:<cursor>, confirmed, duration_ms}` (`confirmed:false` for `unconfirmable`; `duration_ms` runs from the send's arrival, the readiness gate's wait included);
  - or `send-refused{corr:<cursor>, refusal, detail, side:"wrapper", wheel}` with `detail` ∈ `input-not-ready|no-prompt-submitted|turn-running`. `turn-running` has two causes under the one closed detail and no new field: a running turn, or another `send` in flight. The running turn is in-memory wrapper state — marked by a `prompt-submitted` of any origin, ended by `turn-ended` / `session-start` / `session-end` or cleared by a `release` that returns the wheel — and writes no event, span or log line of its own. Either cause's refusal is this wrapper `send-refused` with no `cursor` (`corr` the end offset at refusal, D-28) and no `send-issued`, and the client exits 13;
  - client-side validation refusal, made before any frame: `send-refused{corr:null, refusal:"not-delivered", detail:"control-character"|"empty-text", side:"client"}`, with a mirror line on the wrapper side if the frame reached it. `empty-text` is an empty typed text, read after `control-character` and ahead of both wheel reads; the wrapper, deciding it on a frame sent straight to it, writes its own `send-refused{side:"wrapper"}` line with the same pair and `corr`, `conn` and `rpc_id`, and no `send-issued`. One line per deciding side, never the text;
  - client-side server-verification refusal, made after the client's own refusals and before any frame: no `channel-request` / `channel-response` line on either side; CLI `send` ends `process-exit{subject:"self", exit_code:21, detail:"server-verify-failed", during:"connect"}` at WARN, and MCP `send` writes no line;
  - client-side socket-directory refusal, made after the client's own refusals and before the connect: no `channel-request` / `channel-response` line on either side; CLI `send` ends `process-exit{exit_code:21, detail:"socket-dir-refused", during:"connect"}` at WARN, and MCP `send` writes no line;
  - `channel-response{corr:<id>, conn, result_class, refusal, duration_ms}` on both sides, plus `detail` on a `-32602` only (a word of the closed `unsupported-version|invalid-params|release-from-driver`), absent on every other `channel-response` line, a refusal's included, whose own `detail` stays on `send-refused`;
  - every wrapper `send-*` line (here and in Scenarios 5 and 6) also carries `conn` (or `srv_conn`) and `rpc_id`, so `(conn, rpc_id)` on the send line equals `(conn, corr)` on this call's `channel-*` lines (D-30). The client-side `send-refused{side:"client"}` carries neither.

- **Required log fields:** common fields plus:
  - `channel-request{corr:<id>, conn, method:"wait"|"last"}` on both sides, plus `after` / `timeout_ms` for method `wait` only and only as `u64` values;
  - `channel-response{corr:<id>, conn, result_class, duration_ms}` on both sides, plus `outcome` for method `wait` only: the waking kind (`turn-ended|question|permission|plan|session-end|dialog-expired`, the six of `EventKind::WAIT_WAKE`) or `timed-out`, derived once in `viola-channel` from the result over the shared wake set; the client side alone also writes `instance-unreachable` when the reply never arrived (a closed or reset connection). A `last` response carries no `outcome`, and no result body reaches either line;
  - client `process-exit{subject:"self", exit_code, detail}` at WARN, where exit 21 carries `detail:"instance-dead"` or `detail:"unwrapped-name"` with `during:"connect"`, `detail:"endpoint-lost"` with `during:"call"` (endpoint vanished mid-wait, the wrapper lost with the call open), `detail:"server-verify-failed"` with `during:"connect"` when the serving process is of another euid or not the recorded wrapper, or the check cannot be made, or `detail:"socket-dir-refused"` with `during:"connect"` when the recorded endpoint's socket directory is refused. `wait` / `last`, like `send`, first take the instance check (`client::refuse_untrusted`, before any role file opens), then the liveness-only pre-check, the socket-directory check, the connect, the euid decision and then the server check; a refused instance check exits 21 with the instance pair, or under `--json` exactly `{"v":1,"error":"instance-unreachable","detail":"strict-modes-failed"}`, and sends no frame and writes no line, and MCP `wait` / `last` refused by `check_instance` return that body less `v` (`error` `instance-unreachable`, `detail` `strict-modes-failed`), their text `refused: instance-unreachable`, with no line.
  - `last_assistant_message` never appears.

- **Required log fields:** common fields plus:
  - `hook-invoked{hook_event:"statusline", corr:null}`;
  - `parse-rejected{parser:"hook-stdin", detail:"oversize"|"malformed", count:1}` for stdin the arm rejects (the hook events' own line, written by `reject_stdin` in `src/cmd/hook.rs`);
  - `process-start` / `process-exit{subject:"statusline-shell", shell_exit_status, duration_ms}`, only when the snapshot records a `statusline_command`;
  - `hook-decision{hook_event:"statusline", budget_written, duration_ms}`, plus `detail` ∈ `oversize-stdin|malformed-json|deadline` on a fail-open path, and `deadline_hit` written only when true. `budget_written` is true only when the payload held a `rate_limits` object and the write succeeded;
  - no line at all without a valid `VIOLA_NAME` (as landed, chunk 2026-10-10-statusline-pass-through), and none on an instance whose check refuses: the arm returns exit 0 at once with no role file opened, no `hook-invoked` and no `hook-decision` (as landed, chunk 2026-10-10-budget-governor); and none under the hidden `hook statusline --capture` arm, which runs no instance check, no shell-out and no `budget.json` write and opens no role file (§4 Edge flows);
  - `send-refused{corr:<cursor>, refusal:"budget-paused", detail:"five-hour"|"seven-day", window, used_percentage, resets_at, paused:true}` with client `exit_code:11`.

- **`secret-scan`** (the §6 Error sanitization and secret scan body run in CI before any upload; CI step `id: secret-scan`, obs-plan §9 step 3):
  - Scope: `target/e2e-home/**/diagnostics/*.ndjson` (detail files included), every file under `target/agent-run/` except exactly `target/agent-run/chunk.diff`, and `target/nextest/ci/junit.xml`. `run --mutants`' `chunk.diff` is repository source text by construction (it hits the scan's own needles whenever it touches the scan's source, fresh or stale), and the `harness-<os>` upload excludes the same file, so it is never scanned and never uploaded. A `chunk.diff` anywhere else under the capture is still scanned.
  - Classes:
    - `claude-stripped`: the fixed `CLAUDE*` canaries the root tests plant;
    - `cookie`: the `cookie:` header, case-insensitive;
    - `content-canary`: fails only in a home-level role file;
    - `mode`: Unix only, a diagnostics file that is not `0600`;
    - `unreadable`.
  - A contract test (`crates/viola-e2e/tests/scan_patterns.rs`) keeps the canary list single-sourced: every `canary-<kind>-value-<hex4>` literal in the root `tests/` and `src/` must be in the scan's table.
  - It prints `{"v":1,"cmd":"secret-scan","ok":<bool>,"files":N,"skipped_non_file":N,"mode_check":"unix","hits":[{"file","line","offset","class"}]}`, plus `"report":"unwritten"` when the hit file cannot be written. It never prints the matched bytes.
  - It writes the same document to `target/secret-scan/hits.json` only when there are hits, and deletes a stale one on every run.
  - Reason: `empty-scope`. Exit 0, 1 on any hit, or 2 on usage error.

